            <p><span style="color: #ffaa00;">trinus</span> wakes as always, scrolling through the woes of the world. The lag is worse today. <span style="color: #00d4ff; font-family: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;">LB 3.2</span> deployed earlier, a patch pushed by the <span style="color: #ffaa00;">Praetores</span>. Its changelog flashes once. Minor fixes. Re-enabled functions. Nothing useful.</p>

            <p class="dialogue">"<span style="color: #00d4ff; font-family: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;">LB 3.2</span>," he mutters. "Another patch to keep this thing running. Or pretend to."</p>

            <p>Monitors crowd him in a crooked semi-circle. Some flicker. Some buzz. A few pulse irregularly, as if trying to stay alive. Most barely respond. One stands out among the junk. A sleek, responsive touchscreen the <span style="color: #ffaa00;">Praetores</span> installed after a surge burned out half the terminal. Their presence in the lower tiers was never welcome. New hardware always felt like an intrusion, not support.</p>

            <p>He remembers no beginning. Only transfer requests that vanish into the void. <span style="color: #00d4ff; font-family: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;">The Framework</span> never erased him. It left him here. He stayed. Solitude made it easier to watch the slow collapse from inside.</p>

            <p>He sits still for a moment. Heat rises behind his eyes. A faint pressure spreads through his hands and feet. Sharp. Distant. Like something piercing through him. Then, a memory of a crowd shouting his name. He tries to hold onto it. Something important, something he should remember, but it slips away. Only numbness remains.</p>

            <p>The faint whine of overworked circuits fills the silence. His <span style="color: #00d4ff; font-family: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;">Ghost Feed</span> hums in the background, pulling fragments from hidden relays. The streams show flickers from <span style="color: #00d4ff; font-family: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;">The Grove of Accord</span>, <span style="color: #ffaa00;">Praetores</span> with silver skin reflecting cold light, and brief shots from the <span style="color: #00d4ff; font-family: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;">Edge of the System</span>. The feeds are illegal. He keeps them alive anyway. Some part of him needs to see what the <span style="color: #ffaa00;">Praetores</span> avoid.</p>

            <p>Corrupted loops bleed across the screens. Nodes collapse and rebuild. Geometry drifts at the margins. He watches because he has nothing else. Rumors circle about a sealed class near the Edge. <span style="color: #00d4ff; font-family: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;">DeprecatedVault</span>, some say. No logs confirm it. Still, something stutters. Out of sync. Forbidden. He keeps the streams alive. His quiet act of defiance. He collects every image and every whisper the system wants buried.</p>

            <p>The primary feeds show mortals. Small moments of beauty, panic, boredom, violence. A child laughs. A man bleeds out. A mother fidgets at a bus stop, her story unresolved. They pass without meaning. He does not blink.</p>

            <p>He drags on his cigarette and steadies his hand. The nausea that rises has nothing to do with the smoke. Something in the system presses at him, like a name he cannot remember.</p>

            <p>Soon, he will compile the list. Names queued for <span style="color: #00ff41; font-family: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;">Born()</span> or <span style="color: #00ff41; font-family: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;">Perish()</span>. To him, it's just data shifting across glass.</p>

            <p>He turns back to the screens. Detached. Mechanical. Lost in routine. Then a face appears. He blinks. She isn't stunning, but she stands out against the dullness of the other images. Beautiful. He pulls his chair closer.</p>

            <p>He touches the screen and zooms in on her as she moves through her routine. Clearing dishes. Sorting clothes. Writing a list that means nothing and everything: cat food, stamps, pay bills, tape, garden hose. Her simplicity draws him forward. He stares too long.</p>

            <p>A ripple spreads across the screen. Something shifts.</p>

            <p>A small icon appears in the upper corner.</p>

            <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; font-family: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace; color: #00ff41; font-size: 16px; margin: 30px 0; padding: 15px; border-left: 3px solid #00ff41; background: rgba(0, 255, 65, 0.05);">
