            <p><span style="color: #ffaa00;">trinus</span> gasps. Spins. Rummages through the debris on his desk. Ashtray. Cold coffee. Stacks of paper. Crumpled lists.</p>

            <p class="dialogue">"Where is it? It's here somewhere!"</p>

            <p>Nothing.</p>

            <p>He shoves piles aside. Broken switches. Coils of unused wire. Fried circuit boards. Bins of tech debris. He lifts another box.</p>

            <p class="dialogue">"Ah. There."</p>

            <p>It's an old training manual:<span style="color: #00ff41; font-family: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;"> Functions()</span>. Large, with hundreds of thin, delicate pages. Dog-eared. Coffee-stained. Margins full of scribbles. Slips of paper tucked inside. He flips through it. The index lists <span style="color: #00ff41; font-family: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;">AssignareFatum()</span>, <span style="color: #00ff41; font-family: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;">MortalExpire()</span>, and other usual protocols. All gatekeepers for tallying <span style="color: #ffaa00;">PreBorn</span> for life.</p>

            <p>No <span style="color: #00ff41; font-family: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;">ApostasiaVitae()</span>.</p>

            <p>He tears through the loose pages, scattering them across the floor. One sheet catches his eye. Crisp and untouched. It does not belong here. He flattens it on the desk. A memo.</p>

